(2. Initial Connection Setup) Tj
T*
(1. Place projector on a flat surface between 1.2m and 4.5m from your target wall or projector) Tj
T*
(screen.) Tj
T*
(2. Connect the 19V DC power supply to the main power inlet.) Tj
T*
(3. Connect source devices using high-speed HDMI 2.1 cable to Port 1 \(eARC compatible\).) Tj
T*
(4. Press Power button on top panel or remote control. Allow 15 seconds) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(for optical LED engine warm-up.) Tj
T*
(3. HDMI Connection Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
(Issue 3.1: No HDMI Signal or HDCP Error PRJ-HDMI-01) Tj
T*
(1. Check HDMI source output resolution; ensure output does not exceed 3840x2160 @ 60Hz.) Tj
T*
(2. Perform HDCP handshake reset: Disconnect HDMI cable, turn source device OFF, restart) Tj
T*
(projector, reconnect) Tj
T*
(cable, then turn source device back ON.) Tj
T*
(3. In Settings > Inputs > set HDMI EDID Mode from "Auto" to "HDMI 2.0" or "HDMI 1.4".) Tj
T*
(4. Image Calibration & Distortion Fixes) Tj
T*
(Issue 4.1: Blurry) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Image / Auto-Focus Failure PRJ-IMG-01) Tj
T*
(1. Clean front optical lens with a dry microfiber optical cloth.) Tj
T*
(2. Press Focus + / Focus - on remote to manually override Time-of-Flight \(ToF\) sensor.) Tj
T*
(3. Disable Auto-Focus in Menu > Display > ToF Sensor Calibration.) Tj
T*
(Issue 4.2: Trapezoidal Distortion / Keystone PRJ-IMG-03) Tj
T*
(1. Go to Settings > Projection > 4-Corner Digital Keystone.) Tj
T*
(2. Use direction arrows on remote control to manually align all four corner boundaries until) Tj
T*
(screen rectangular ratio) Tj
T*
(is) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(restored.) Tj
T*
